{title: Lineage of Judah}
{subtitle: 1 Chronicles 2:48; 2:42–50; 2:18–20}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Roots go deep in the promised land
Where the [B]shadows of [F#]ancestors [C#]stand
[D#m]Caleb son of Hezron strong
[B]His lineage is [C#]the song we [D#m]sing
Azubah bore the sons of light
[B]Jesher Shobab and [F#]Ardon [C#]tight
But [D#m]when she died he found new grace
Ephrath bore [B]the Hur who [C#]has a [D#m]place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Maacah bore the sons of [B]the line
Sheber and Tirhanah alig[F#]ned
Through the concubine the blood flows on
In [C#]the genealogy of Judah [D#m]known
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Ephah brought Haran Moza and Gazez
Harans fa[B]ther the one who [F#]came in [C#]last
Jahdai [D#m]sons like Regem and Jotham
Geshan Pe[B]let Ephah [C#]standing [D#m]out
Maacah again with Sheber and Tirhanah
Shaaph [B]the father of [F#]Madman[C#]nah
Sheva fa[D#m]ther of Macbenah too
And Gibea [B]rises in [C#]the [D#m]dew
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Maacah bore the sons of the line
[B]Sheber and Tirhanah alig[F#]ned
Through the concubine the blood flows on
In [C#]the genealogy of Judah [D#m]known
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Caleb daughter Acsah stands apart
In the [B]record of the [F#]fathers [C#]heart
De[D#m]scendants of Caleb clear to see
The [B]tribe of Ju[C#]dah set [D#m]free
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
These are the descendants of Caleb
The [B]sons of Hur the [F#]firstborn of Ep[C#]hrathah
Shobal fa[D#m]ther of Kiriath Jearim
The [B]line is marked for [C#]all to [D#m]hear
{end_of_verse}

